## Scope Contract 1: Unbounded GROQ Queries — Gap #2 (CRITICAL)

### Target State
All product queries have bounded results with pagination support. No query returns >200 products. Cursor-based pagination available for large datasets.

### DoD (Definition of Done)

**Pass 1: Skeleton (Schema & Interface)**
- [ ] Add `MAX_PRODUCTS_LIMIT = 200` constant
- [ ] Define `GetProductsOptions` interface with `cursor?: string | null` and `limit?: number`
- [ ] Define `ProductsResponse` interface with `products`, `nextCursor`, `hasMore`

**Pass 2: Data (Query Implementation)**
- [ ] Update `getProductsByVfsKeys.ts` to accept options object
- [ ] Add slice syntax `[0...$limit]` to GROQ query
- [ ] Implement cursor-based pagination logic
- [ ] Return `nextCursor` and `hasMore` in response

**Pass 3: Build (Integration & Testing)**
- [ ] Layer 1: Structure — Update function signature, no styling
- [ ] Layer 2: Layout — Error boundary positioning
- [ ] Layer 3: Surface — Loading states for pagination
- [ ] Layer 4: Interaction — "Load More" button behavior
- [ ] Desktop (1280px): Pagination controls positioned correctly
- [ ] Mobile (375px): Touch-friendly pagination

### Verification

```bash
# Build gate
npm run build

# Specification tests
npx vitest run tests/catalogue/pagination.test.ts

# Runtime verification
npm run test:perf -- --category=headphones
# Expected: TTFB < 500ms, max 200 products returned
```

### Files Modified
- `@/sanity/lib/products/getProductsByVfsKeys.ts`
- `@/app/(store)/products/[...slug]/page.tsx` (integration)
- `@/app/components/skeletons/ProductGridSkeleton.tsx` (new)

