## Scope Contract 3: Dynamic Filter Configuration — Gap #4 (HIGH)

### Target State
Filter options are fetched from CMS/product data, not hardcoded. FilterSidebar displays real available filters per category.

### DoD (Definition of Done)

**Pass 1: Skeleton (Data Layer)**
- [ ] Update `FilterConfigProvider` to accept `categoryKeys` prop
- [ ] Import `getFiltersForCategoryPathAction` from actions
- [ ] Define filter extraction query interface

**Pass 2: Data (Implementation)**
- [ ] Replace mockFilters with dynamic fetch: `getFiltersForCategoryPathAction(categoryKeys)`
- [ ] Implement filter extraction from products (brand, driverType, etc.)
- [ ] Add deduplication and sorting of filter options
- [ ] Handle empty/no-filter categories

**Pass 3: Build (Integration)**
- [ ] Layer 1: Structure — Update page.tsx to pass categoryKeys
- [ ] Layer 2: Layout — Filter sidebar width unchanged
- [ ] Layer 3: Surface — Loading state for filters
- [ ] Layer 4: Interaction — Filter selection instant feedback
- [ ] Desktop (1280px): Filter sidebar renders with real options
- [ ] Mobile (375px): Mobile filter drawer with real options

### Verification

```bash
# Build gate
npm run build

# Specification tests
npx vitest run tests/catalogue/dynamic-filters.test.ts
npx vitest run tests/component/FilterConfigProvider.spec.tsx

# Runtime verification
