## Scope Contract 4: Server-Side Sorting — Gap #5 (HIGH)

### Target State
Sorting happens on server via GROQ, not client-side. No main-thread blocking on large product sets.

### DoD (Definition of Done)

**Pass 1: Skeleton (URL Integration)**
- [ ] Update `SortDropdown` to use `shallow: false` for full page reload
- [ ] Remove client-side sort state management
- [ ] Verify sort param reaches server component

**Pass 2: Data (Server Implementation)**
- [ ] Confirm `getProductsByVfsKeys` accepts sort parameter (already implemented)
- [ ] Remove client-side sorting from `CategoryPageClient`
- [ ] Verify GROQ `order()` clause applies correctly

**Pass 3: Build (UI Polish)**
- [ ] Layer 1: Structure — Sort dropdown unchanged
- [ ] Layer 2: Layout — Loading state positioning
- [ ] Layer 3: Surface — Sort active state styling
- [ ] Layer 4: Interaction — Transition feedback during sort
- [ ] Desktop (1280px): Sort dropdown functional
- [ ] Mobile (375px): Mobile sort dropdown functional

### Verification

```bash
# Build gate
npm run build

# Specification tests
npx vitest run tests/catalogue/server-sort.test.ts
npx vitest run tests/component/SortDropdown.spec.tsx

# Performance verification
npm run test:perf -- --category=headphones
# Expected: No main-thread jank when sorting 200+ products
```

### Files Modified
- `@/app/components/features/filters/SortDropdown.tsx`
- `@/app/(store)/products/[...slug]/CategoryPageClient.tsx`
- `@/app/(store)/products/[...slug]/page.tsx`

