## Scope Contract 8: Brand Data Model — Gap #1 (CRITICAL)

### Target State
Brand is a reference document type, not a string. All products reference brand documents. Filtering works consistently across brand name variations.

### DoD (Definition of Done)

**Pass 1: Skeleton (Schema Definition)**
- [ ] Create `@/sanity/schemaTypes/brandType.ts`
- [ ] Define fields: `name`, `slug`, `logo`
- [ ] Update `productType.ts` brand field to reference type
- [ ] Add brandType to sanity.config.ts schemaTypes

**Pass 2: Data (Migration)**
- [ ] Create migration script: `scripts/migrate-brands.mjs`
- [ ] Extract unique brand strings from all products
- [ ] Create brand documents (normalized names)
- [ ] Update all products to reference correct brand
- [ ] Validate all products have valid brand reference

**Pass 3: Build (Query & Component Updates)**
- [ ] Layer 1: Structure — Update GROQ projections: `brand-> { _id, name, slug }`
- [ ] Layer 2: Layout — Update ProductCard brand display positioning
- [ ] Layer 3: Surface — Brand logo rendering in product cards
- [ ] Layer 4: Interaction — Brand link hover states
- [ ] Desktop (1280px): Brand display in grid layout
- [ ] Mobile (375px): Brand display in compact layout

### Verification

```bash
# Build gate
npm run build

# Migration verification
node scripts/migrate-brands.mjs --dry-run

# Specification tests
npx vitest run tests/catalogue/brand-reference.test.ts
npx vitest run tests/component/ProductCard.spec.tsx

# Filter integration
npx playwright test --grep "brand-filter"
```

### Files Modified
- `@/sanity/schemaTypes/brandType.ts` (new)
- `@/sanity/schemaTypes/productType.ts`
- `@/sanity/config.ts`
- `@/scripts/migrate-brands.mjs` (new)
- `@/sanity/lib/products/getProductsByVfsKeys.ts`
- `@/app/components/product/ProductCard.tsx`
- `@/app/components/filters/FilterSidebar.tsx`

